Interpretation of the Coefficients
Nightly price has a positive coefficient of 48.53. In the model, a one-dollar increase in
nightly price is associated with approximately $48.53 more estimated annual revenue, holding
the other included variables constant. The p-value is very small and the reported 95% confidence
interval is positive, from $30.95 to $66.11. This is consistent with the positive relationship
shown in the scatterplot, although the coefficient should not be treated as a guaranteed return
from increasing a listing’s price.
Guest capacity has a positive coefficient of $3,796.28. Each additional guest the property
accommodates is associated with approximately $3,796 more estimated annual revenue, holding
